# 1. Purpose

This policy established the underwriting standards used by Meridian Financial Services to evaluate consumer loan applications during the 2024 policy period.

This document is retained for historical reference and audit purposes.

It is **not the current underwriting policy**.

---

# 2. Scope

This policy applied to consumer loan applications submitted through Meridian Financial Services during the period beginning January 1, 2024.

The policy covered:

* Personal loans
* Auto loans
* Debt-consolidation loans
* Home-improvement loans

---

# 3. Applicant Eligibility

## 3.1 Minimum Income

Applicants were generally required to demonstrate annual income of at least **$35,000**.

Certain loan products could establish higher requirements.

## 3.2 Employment History

Applicants were generally expected to demonstrate at least **6 months of continuous employment history**.

Applications with shorter employment histories could be referred for manual review.

## 3.3 Credit Risk Tier

The credit risk tiers used during this policy period were:

* Tier A
* Tier B
* Tier C
* Tier D

Product-specific requirements determined which tiers qualified for automatic approval.

---

# 4. Loan Amount Requirements

## 4.1 Maximum Loan Amount

Maximum loan amounts were determined by the applicable loan-product rules.

## 4.2 High-Dollar Applications

Applications requesting more than **$40,000** were generally subject to manual review.

---

# 5. Debt-to-Income Review

Applications were evaluated against product-specific debt-to-income thresholds.

Applications exceeding the applicable threshold could be referred for manual review.

---

# 6. Product Eligibility

Applicants were required to meet the product-specific eligibility requirements in effect at the time of the application.

The product rules included:

* Minimum credit tier
* Minimum income
* Maximum loan amount
* Debt-to-income threshold
* Geographic eligibility
* Review requirements

---

# 7. Fair-Lending Requirements

## 7.1 Consistent Evaluation

Applicants were required to be evaluated according to applicable underwriting criteria.

## 7.2 Documentation

Material underwriting decisions were expected to have a documented business justification.

## 7.3 Compliance Review

Potential compliance concerns could be referred to the Compliance team for additional review.

---

# 8. Automated Decisions

Eligible applications could receive an automated approval or decline when all required information was available and the applicable underwriting criteria were satisfied.

Applications outside automated thresholds were referred for manual review.

---

# 9. Manual Review

Manual review was generally required when:

* Required information was missing.
* The requested amount exceeded $40,000.
* The applicant did not clearly satisfy an automated approval requirement.
* Credit information required additional review.
* Product-specific rules required manual review.

---

# 10. Historical Status

This policy was effective from **January 1, 2024 through December 31, 2025**.

On January 1, 2026, Version 2.0 became effective and replaced this document.

This document must not be used as the controlling policy for applications evaluated under the 2026 underwriting framework.

For current decisions, retrieve:

